    "content": "1\t# Task 11: Floating islands in a sunset sky\n2\t\n3\tBuild a single-page browser app with the provided framework, served by vite. It must render one full-viewport canvas with id #app. The scene is a sky full of floating rock islands at sunset. Show at least 6 islands of different sizes, each a chunky rock underside tapering downward (cone or inverted-lump shapes) topped with a grassy surface and a few simple trees or crystals. Islands bob gently up and down at different speeds and phases. A warm orange to pink gradient sky fills the background with a large low sun, and 8 or more soft cloud banks drift slowly past at different depths. A thin waterfall or particle stream falls from the largest island. Distance haze makes far islands paler and bluer. The camera slowly drifts in a wide arc, looping every 40 to 60 seconds, with no user input. Do not rely on external downloads; build everything procedurally. Keep it above 30 fps on a mid-range laptop.\n4\t\n5\tThe rendering contract in the next section applies.\n6\t\n7\t## Rendering contract (all tasks)\n8\t\n9\t- Draw into the existing `<canvas id=\"app\">` (640x360 CSS pixels, device pixel ratio 1). Do not resize it or create another canvas.\n10\t- Render continuously with `requestAnimationFrame`. When the first frame has been drawn set `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true`.\n11\t- No network access: load assets only from `/assets/...` (served from `public/assets`). Do not import from CDNs.\n12\t- Code goes in `src/` (TypeScript, strict). The entry is `src/m"
